HOL4 conditional/contextual simplifier
======================================

The ordinary simplifier is simpLib/congLib, built on Traverse, Cond_rewr,
Opening and Travrules, with the pureSimps/boolSimps/combinSimps fragments.
Loading these does not load the extension engine, its strategy state,
source inventories or split persistence.

The extension engine is opt-in. Its clients use the simpExtLib/TraverseExt
types; ordinary fragments and simpsets enter by simpExtLib.lift_ssfrag/
lift_simpset. Configured congruence uses congExtLib; threaded factories are
Opening.THREADED_CONGPROC and Travrules.mk_threaded_travrules; paired
conditional compilation uses Cond_rewrExt. Both engines share TraverseCore,
congLibFn and simpCommon.

Documentation:
  src/notes.md                           types, engines and controls
  src/MANIFEST                           defining modules and dependency rules
  tests/api-audit/Documentation.sml      executable typed examples
  tests/simp-ext/APIExamples.sml         configured/global tactic examples
  help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.*.smd         extension reference (repository root)

From the repository root:
  bin/Holmake --holstate="$PWD/bin/hol.state0" \
    -C src/simp/src -j1 HOLSELFTESTLEVEL=1 all

The ordinary selftest.sml does not import the extension engine. Extension
tests, public source clients and fresh-load/persistence fixtures have
independent processes and normal-level targets. After list theories are
built, the normal build sequence runs tests/native-extension again,
including the option/pair/list cases that the earlier run skips.

Persistent [split] declarations require explicit splitPersistLib loading and
Theory.add_ML_dependency "splitPersistLib" on the earliest declaring theory.
